WEBVTT

00:04.320 --> 00:06.880
I know you hate it
when I review the game tapes...

00:07.057 --> 00:09.753
...but that was one for the highlight reel.

00:10.627 --> 00:12.288
The highlight reel?

00:12.462 --> 00:17.422
Yeah, you know,
best-of moments for deathbed reflections.

00:17.934 --> 00:19.925
Only in your memory, right?

00:20.103 --> 00:23.766
Oh, yeah, yeah.
I got rid of the camcorder like I promised.

00:23.940 --> 00:25.567
Good.

00:25.742 --> 00:28.734
It's a shame.
The camera really loves you.

00:28.912 --> 00:32.643
- Shut up, Charlie.
- I'm not just saying that.

00:32.816 --> 00:36.843
Even from unflattering angles,
you light up the screen.

00:37.020 --> 00:38.783
Oh, I hate you.

00:38.955 --> 00:42.152
That's too bad, because I love you.

00:48.431 --> 00:49.921
Really?

00:54.871 --> 00:56.065
Um...

00:57.006 --> 00:59.941
...actually, yes.

01:00.577 --> 01:02.340
Yes, I do.

01:02.512 --> 01:04.002
I love you, Chelsea.

01:05.415 --> 01:07.713
Oh, that's so sweet.

01:08.418 --> 01:09.544
Thank you.

01:17.827 --> 01:20.387
No, no, thank you.

01:51.227 --> 01:52.524
Morning.

01:53.096 --> 01:54.996
Always gotta make a comment,
don't you?

01:57.233 --> 02:01.533
Oh, my.
Fitful night's sleep on Alcohol Island?

02:02.639 --> 02:04.004
Keep it up, funny man.

02:04.174 --> 02:06.301
You're gonna be homeless,
wearing a tube top...

02:06.476 --> 02:08.740
...and turning tricks
on Santa Monica Boulevard.

02:09.813 --> 02:12.748
Wow, what crawled in your keister
and built a nest?

02:12.916 --> 02:14.816
You wanna know?
You really wanna know?

02:16.319 --> 02:18.014
I've fallen in love with Chelsea.

02:18.388 --> 02:22.347
Oh, well, why are you so upset?
Uh, love is a- A beautiful thing.

02:22.525 --> 02:24.755
Beautiful thing, my ass.

02:25.528 --> 02:27.018
And we're back in your keister.

02:30.033 --> 02:34.367
Last night in bed, I told her I loved her,
and you know what she said?

02:34.938 --> 02:37.702
Uh, "I'm still not gonna
let you do that"?

02:44.647 --> 02:46.376
She said, "Thank you."

02:47.750 --> 02:49.877
Ooh, that's an ice cube
to the man sack.

02:53.056 --> 02:54.421
I don't get it.

02:54.591 --> 02:57.617
I've gone the whole 9 yards
for this relationship.

02:57.794 --> 03:02.060
I gave her her own drawer in my bedroom.
I stopped smoking cigars after sex.

03:02.232 --> 03:04.496
I started seeing a shrink
so I could be sensitive.

03:04.667 --> 03:06.635
I still can't get a freaking "I love you."

03:06.803 --> 03:09.636
But you've obviously
become more sensitive.

03:11.040 --> 03:13.975
For what I've spent on therapy,
I could get expensive hookers...

03:14.143 --> 03:16.611
...who will say anything I want.

03:17.213 --> 03:19.738
There's that sensitivity again.

03:19.916 --> 03:20.940
Look on the bright side.

03:22.318 --> 03:24.650
- The bright side?
- When women do tell you they love you...

03:24.821 --> 03:29.087
...it usually ends with them tossing a lit
road flare through your bedroom window.

03:30.293 --> 03:32.261
That happened one time.

03:32.428 --> 03:34.589
Why can't you be grateful
for what you've got?

03:34.764 --> 03:37.733
- What do I got?
- A woman who may not proclaim her love...

03:37.901 --> 03:41.029
...but who doesn't try to set you on fire
while you're sleeping.

03:41.437 --> 03:42.665
One time.

03:43.606 --> 03:47.565
A woman who may not proclaim her love
but who doesn't steal your Mercedes...

03:47.744 --> 03:51.441
...while you're passed out in the back seat
and drive it into the Pacific Ocean.

03:52.282 --> 03:54.477
Another isolated incident.

03:55.685 --> 03:57.084
I believe I've made my point.

03:58.488 --> 04:02.254
I'm sorry, Alan, but not being drowned
or burned by the woman I love...

04:02.425 --> 04:03.790
...is not enough for me.

04:04.227 --> 04:06.320
I want more.

04:07.497 --> 04:10.898
Oh, sure, reach for the stars.

04:17.507 --> 04:21.204
- Hey, Charlie, how's it going?
- Boy, you really blew it this time.

04:23.212 --> 04:25.180
Did I, now? How so?

04:27.183 --> 04:28.673
I've fallen in love with Chelsea.

04:29.652 --> 04:31.711
Ooh, my bad.

04:32.121 --> 04:33.645
Damn right, your bad.

04:33.823 --> 04:36.815
Plenty of medications
would've turned me into a happy potato...

04:36.993 --> 04:39.154
...but would you prescribe them? No.

04:40.463 --> 04:42.454
You said to get in touch
with my feelings...

04:42.632 --> 04:45.192
...and express them
to the people I care about.

04:45.568 --> 04:48.298
Sorry, I must have been drunk.

04:48.471 --> 04:51.463
No, no, no. It's too late for excuses.

04:52.008 --> 04:54.568
I'm sensing something happened
with Chelsea.

04:54.744 --> 04:58.475
Oh, you're good.
There's no sliding anything past you.

04:59.015 --> 05:01.609
Hey, last night I dreamt
I was a giant hot dog...

05:01.784 --> 05:04.412
...jumping through a doughnut
that looked like my mother.

05:04.587 --> 05:06.248
What do you suppose that means?

05:07.056 --> 05:10.423
All right, Charlie, you've made your point.
Now tell me what happened.

05:10.593 --> 05:12.686
We can go back
to the doughnut dream later.

05:12.862 --> 05:15.023
It wasn't a real dream.
I was being sarcastic.

05:15.198 --> 05:19.396
Oh, I know, but the fact that you chose
that particular imagery is a little troubling.

05:20.103 --> 05:21.536
Now, what happened with Chelsea?

05:22.205 --> 05:24.571
I told her I loved her,
and you know what she said?

05:24.741 --> 05:27.608
This process isn't really about
me guessing, Charlie.

05:29.512 --> 05:31.241
She said, "Thank you."

05:32.015 --> 05:34.415
Interesting. How did that make you feel?

05:34.584 --> 05:38.315
No, no, no. No more feelings.
We tried it your way.

05:38.488 --> 05:41.286
Now just take out your prescription pad
and start scribbling.

05:41.457 --> 05:43.118
You don't need medication, Charlie.

05:43.292 --> 05:45.385
You're actually
making tremendous progress.

05:45.561 --> 05:49.691
- Are you not listening to a thing I say?
- I drift in and out.

05:51.634 --> 05:54.432
The fact that you're upset
tells me you've come a long way...

05:54.604 --> 05:57.038
...from the guy
who first walked into this office.

05:57.206 --> 05:59.197
The guy who first walked
into this office...

05:59.375 --> 06:03.243
...was a happy-go-lucky, fully functioning
man-whore, and I want him back.

06:03.746 --> 06:05.611
I'm guessing you don't mean that.

06:05.782 --> 06:08.250
Oh, now you're guessing?
A minute ago it was:

06:08.418 --> 06:11.444
- "That's not how the process works."
- A minute ago it didn't.

06:14.690 --> 06:16.248
So are you still seeing Chelsea?

06:17.393 --> 06:22.262
Of course I'm still seeing her,
but now the relationship's totally screwed.

06:22.432 --> 06:24.900
- Why is that?
- She knows I love her.

06:25.068 --> 06:28.435
The whole balance of power
is completely out of whack.

06:28.905 --> 06:29.929
Huh.

06:30.673 --> 06:33.403
Okay, I really don't like it
when you give me the "huh."

06:34.177 --> 06:35.667
Huh.

06:36.245 --> 06:40.705
- Now you're just screwing with me, right?
- There's no sliding anything past you.

06:42.618 --> 06:46.418
So let's talk about this whole
"balance of power" issue of yours.

06:46.889 --> 06:48.948
- What about it?
- Why look at relationships...

06:49.125 --> 06:50.183
...as a power struggle?

06:50.660 --> 06:52.491
Because that's what they are.

06:52.662 --> 06:55.187
You saw your parents' relationship
as a power struggle?

06:55.364 --> 06:56.661
Oh, there was no struggle.

06:56.833 --> 07:00.667
My father sat very quietly
while my mother sucked the life out of him.

07:01.137 --> 07:04.197
I see, and you're terrified
of that happening to you.

07:04.373 --> 07:06.841
No, I'm looking forward to it.

07:08.044 --> 07:10.512
Thinking about having a nozzle
attached to my heart...

07:10.680 --> 07:12.841
...to make the sucking more convenient.

07:13.950 --> 07:15.110
Let me ask you something.

07:15.284 --> 07:19.414
What would it take for you to feel that
things were back in balance with Chelsea?

07:19.589 --> 07:22.854
- Simple. She has to tell me she loves me.
- Even if she doesn't feel it?

07:23.426 --> 07:25.826
It's even better if she doesn't feel it...

07:27.130 --> 07:31.294
...because that means she's only saying it
because she's afraid to lose me.

07:31.901 --> 07:32.959
Wow.

07:33.636 --> 07:34.830
Wow?

07:35.004 --> 07:36.028
What's "wow"?

07:36.205 --> 07:39.538
Kind of like "huh" but with a
"wuh" and an "ow."

07:42.345 --> 07:45.576
I would suggest that you forget
about getting the "I love you" back...

07:45.748 --> 07:48.342
...and focus more on what it feels like
to give love...

07:48.518 --> 07:50.645
...maybe for the first time in your life.

07:52.889 --> 07:56.450
You know,
I can get the drugs without you.

07:57.326 --> 07:59.886
I got a nephew in junior high.

08:01.898 --> 08:03.957
Do what you gotta do.

08:04.133 --> 08:07.068
Now let's get back
to that mom-shaped doughnut of yours.

08:12.375 --> 08:16.243
- So you really told her you loved her?
- Yeah.

08:16.412 --> 08:18.346
Were you loaded?

08:19.382 --> 08:20.974
- No.
- Were you trying to get her...

08:21.150 --> 08:23.050
...to do something kinky?

08:24.020 --> 08:26.215
- No.
- Did she catch you doing something kinky...

08:26.389 --> 08:27.947
...to somebody else?

08:30.026 --> 08:32.460
- No.
- By yourself?

08:32.628 --> 08:33.856
No.

08:34.030 --> 08:36.464
Then I don't get it. What was your angle?

08:37.233 --> 08:39.030
My angle was I love her.

08:39.368 --> 08:40.460
Huh.

08:41.237 --> 08:44.229
Why does everybody go "huh"?
What's with the "huh"?

08:44.407 --> 08:47.774
- We always knew this day would come.
- What day?

08:48.244 --> 08:51.008
The day you stopped manipulating
and conning women.

08:51.180 --> 08:54.707
The day you dropped your guard
and let an honest emotion into your heart.

08:55.418 --> 08:56.612
That's a good day, right?

08:56.786 --> 08:59.448
If you don't mind
being some broad's prison bitch.

09:05.928 --> 09:07.225
What are you gonna do now?

09:08.764 --> 09:09.788
I don't know.

09:09.966 --> 09:13.163
I can't keep seeing her,
because the relationship's out of balance...

09:13.336 --> 09:15.668
...and I can't stop seeing her,
because I love her.

09:16.205 --> 09:17.832
I feel for you.

09:18.007 --> 09:20.066
I once loved a guy
who didn't love me back.

09:20.243 --> 09:22.973
- What did you do?
- Ninety days in county.

09:24.580 --> 09:26.639
Plus anger-management classes...

09:26.816 --> 09:30.252
...which, by the way,
are a total freaking waste of time.

09:39.061 --> 09:41.325
- Hey.
- Hey.

09:45.001 --> 09:46.491
Have you ever been in love?

09:54.910 --> 09:55.934
Hey, Alan.

09:56.112 --> 09:58.103
Ocupado.

09:59.515 --> 10:02.609
I got it, I got it, I got it.

10:02.785 --> 10:05.345
I know how to restore the balance of power
with Chelsea.

10:05.521 --> 10:08.684
&lt;i>Excuse me. What part of "ocupado"
don't you understand?&lt;/i>

10:08.858 --> 10:11.326
&lt;i>The "ocu" or the "pado "?&lt;/i>

10:12.128 --> 10:14.858
I understood it all,
I was just hoping you were shaving.

10:15.298 --> 10:18.290
Well, I'm not, and as you well know,
this is an uphill battle for me...

10:18.467 --> 10:20.230
...even in the best of circumstances.

10:20.403 --> 10:22.496
Yeah, yeah, yeah, but this is important.

10:22.672 --> 10:24.640
I'm gonna get an "I love you"
from Chelsea.

10:24.807 --> 10:28.004
If you let me finish,
you'll get one from me.

10:31.414 --> 10:33.314
Check this out.

10:34.950 --> 10:37.180
Oh, Charlie, this is so sudden.

10:41.724 --> 10:44.591
If you'll wait a few minutes,
I'll have a gift for you.

10:52.902 --> 10:55.894
- I'm gonna marry Chelsea.
- Are you serious?

10:56.072 --> 10:59.337
Serious enough to ignore what's going on
right in front of me.

11:02.445 --> 11:06.677
- Well, congratulations, I guess.
- Thank you.

11:06.849 --> 11:10.341
Let's see her not say "I love you" now.

11:14.256 --> 11:16.451
Let's see what marriage does
to his bowels.

11:26.769 --> 11:28.862
- How's your salmon?
- Delicious.

11:29.038 --> 11:32.371
- This is such a romantic restaurant.
- I'm glad you like it.

11:33.609 --> 11:36.601
- Have you been here before?
- No.

11:38.681 --> 11:40.148
Yes.

11:41.517 --> 11:43.109
Well, a couple times.

11:44.820 --> 11:46.378
A lot.

11:49.725 --> 11:52.558
I know you've dated other women.
Why would you lie?

11:53.028 --> 11:54.723
Survival instinct.

11:54.897 --> 11:57.661
Same reason I don't drink
in the bathtub anymore.

11:58.100 --> 11:59.863
What else have you lied to me about?

12:00.369 --> 12:02.997
I don't know.
What else haven't you believed?

12:03.172 --> 12:04.332
You're awful.

12:04.707 --> 12:07.733
- Awful good, right?
- Yeah.

12:07.910 --> 12:09.901
Excuse me, I have to powder my nose.

12:10.813 --> 12:12.542
Okay, who's lying now?

12:16.218 --> 12:17.310
Bobby.

12:19.555 --> 12:20.817
Is everything all right?

12:20.990 --> 12:23.083
Yeah, terrific.
My date's in the ladies' room.

12:23.259 --> 12:25.386
- I need you to do something.
- Not a problem.

12:25.561 --> 12:28.189
I'll have the valet bring your car around
to the alley...

12:28.364 --> 12:31.060
...I'll open the men's room window
so you can shimmy out...

12:31.233 --> 12:33.224
...and I'll have a cab
take the lady home...

12:33.402 --> 12:36.838
...along with the customary
chocolate soufflé to go.

12:37.006 --> 12:40.874
No, no, no, I'm not breaking up with her.
I'm gonna ask her to marry me.

12:41.677 --> 12:43.770
I think we need to get some coffee
in you.

12:45.948 --> 12:48.109
I'm not drunk.
I know exactly what I'm doing.

12:48.284 --> 12:50.081
As always.

12:50.252 --> 12:54.188
All I need you to do is bring champagne,
pour a glass for her and a glass for me...

12:54.356 --> 12:57.257
...then distract her
so I can slip the ring into her glass.

12:57.426 --> 12:59.621
Oh, how charmingly original.

13:00.529 --> 13:02.963
- You've seen that before?
- Never.

13:04.834 --> 13:06.893
Here she comes. Go get the champagne.

13:07.069 --> 13:09.867
I'll keep the bathroom window open
just in case.

13:11.407 --> 13:13.841
Charlie, there's something
I wanna talk to you about.

13:14.009 --> 13:15.476
Okay.

13:17.546 --> 13:20.913
The other day when you said you loved me,
I didn't really respond.

13:21.083 --> 13:24.382
Yes, you did. You said, "Thank you."
You were very courteous.

13:25.387 --> 13:27.719
It's not that I don't have strong feelings
for you.

13:27.890 --> 13:30.916
It's just that taking that extra step
is really hard for me.

13:31.093 --> 13:32.355
Well, don't worry about it.

13:32.528 --> 13:36.294
I'm sure you'll take that step
when it's appropriate. Oh, look, champagne.

13:37.766 --> 13:39.233
Ooh, is it a special occasion?

13:39.401 --> 13:43.337
- Every night with you is a special occasion.
- I'm going to miss you, sir.

13:46.542 --> 13:47.600
&lt;i>Go do the thing.&lt;/i>

13:50.045 --> 13:54.072
Oh, dear.
I hope I'm not having a massive coronary.

13:56.785 --> 13:59.481
- Oh, my God, are you all right?
- I'm not sure.

14:00.489 --> 14:02.252
Yes, I'm fine.

14:03.726 --> 14:06.160
The one waiter in L.A.
who's not an actor.

14:06.328 --> 14:07.989
- What?
- Uh, nothing. Nothing.

14:09.365 --> 14:10.764
A toast.

14:10.933 --> 14:12.366
To saying what we feel.

14:20.442 --> 14:22.376
What the hell did I just swallow?

14:22.878 --> 14:25.642
- A one-bedroom condo.
- What?

14:26.048 --> 14:28.881
I put a diamond ring
in your champagne glass.

14:29.318 --> 14:31.878
- Why?
- What do you mean, "why"?

14:32.054 --> 14:35.854
I was gonna propose, and I had no idea
you'd chug it like a Jell-O shot.

14:36.025 --> 14:39.825
- That was a ring I just swallowed?
- Who drinks champagne like that?

14:40.396 --> 14:42.887
I was thirsty. Stop yelling at me.

14:43.065 --> 14:45.693
How in God's name
could you swallow it so easily?

14:45.868 --> 14:48.701
Hey, that's one of the things you love
about me.

14:50.372 --> 14:52.237
- Problem?
- No problem. Go away.

14:52.408 --> 14:53.898
Car's outside, window's open.

14:55.177 --> 14:57.008
- Let's go.
- Where?

14:57.179 --> 14:59.147
- The emergency room.
- Why?

14:59.315 --> 15:01.749
Because I have a ring in my stomach.

15:02.217 --> 15:05.084
- Oh, don't worry about that. You'll be fine.
- How do you know?

15:05.254 --> 15:08.712
When Jake was little, he swallowed nickels.
Nothing bad happened.

15:09.191 --> 15:11.022
- Are you sure?
- Absolutely.

15:11.193 --> 15:13.753
He still shoots one out
every now and then.

15:13.929 --> 15:15.226
Bets me heads or tails.

15:17.800 --> 15:21.065
Just between you and me,
I'm even not sure they're the same nickels.

15:22.571 --> 15:24.232
Trust me.

15:24.406 --> 15:27.102
Couple of cups of coffee in the morning,
problem solved.

15:28.777 --> 15:31.075
I suppose you're right.

15:32.414 --> 15:34.939
- So, what do you say?
- What do I say about what?

15:35.117 --> 15:37.881
- I asked you to marry me.
- No, you didn't.

15:38.053 --> 15:40.283
I was about to
until you ruined the moment.

15:40.456 --> 15:42.185
I ruined the moment?

15:42.358 --> 15:44.758
Okay, okay,
there's no sense in assigning blame.

15:46.629 --> 15:48.790
The point is, I'm proposing.

15:50.833 --> 15:53.802
- You wanna marry me?
- Yes. I love you.

15:55.671 --> 15:59.368
- I don't know what to say.
- Say you love me and you'll marry me.

16:00.643 --> 16:03.043
Charlie, you're kind of putting me
on the spot here.

16:03.212 --> 16:06.978
Yeah, well, that's kind of built in
to the whole proposal concept.

16:07.583 --> 16:09.949
Oh, come on,
just say it so we can be even.

16:10.119 --> 16:13.555
Even? Is that what this is about?
Some kind of power thing?

16:14.089 --> 16:18.389
No, no, no, I meant
"so that we can be even closer."

16:19.028 --> 16:20.154
Right.

16:20.796 --> 16:22.593
Okay, that was lame.

16:22.765 --> 16:24.995
- But don't blame me, blame my shrink.
- What?

16:25.167 --> 16:28.568
If I was properly medicated
we wouldn't be having this conversation.

16:29.638 --> 16:32.163
Boy, this keeps getting
more and more romantic.

16:32.608 --> 16:34.974
Look, do you love me or not?

16:36.178 --> 16:37.668
- I guess so.
- No guessing.

16:37.846 --> 16:39.473
That's not how the process works.

16:41.417 --> 16:42.441
All right, I love you.

16:42.618 --> 16:45.985
Well, great. Great, good.
That's all I wanted.

16:46.488 --> 16:48.956
- But I won't marry you.
- What?

16:49.124 --> 16:51.388
Oh, yeah, right. That's okay, no biggie.

16:55.030 --> 16:57.760
I just got out of a marriage.
I'm not ready to do it again.

16:57.933 --> 16:59.195
That's fine. I understand.

16:59.635 --> 17:02.160
I'm not saying no.
I'm just saying not now.

17:02.705 --> 17:05.037
Hey, "not now" is my favorite time
for a wedding.

17:07.342 --> 17:09.469
The important thing
is that we love each other.

17:09.645 --> 17:11.112
- Right.
- Equally.

17:11.280 --> 17:13.111
- Yes.
- Fifty-fifty.

17:14.016 --> 17:16.246
If it means that much to you.

17:16.418 --> 17:20.149
Come on, say it again. "I love you."

17:20.823 --> 17:22.950
- No.
- Why not?

17:23.125 --> 17:25.491
I wanna see the ring first.

17:32.134 --> 17:33.624
Hey, Berta.

17:33.802 --> 17:36.930
Where do we keep
the spaghetti-strainer thingy?

17:37.606 --> 17:40.666
It's called a colander.
What do you need it for?

17:40.843 --> 17:43.403
It's not for me, it's for Chelsea.

17:45.047 --> 17:49.177
Okay, what kind of Martha Stewart
freak show you got going on up there?

17:49.685 --> 17:54.315
- Trust me, you don't need the details.
- I don't want the details.

17:54.490 --> 17:58.517
I just need to know whether to wash it
or throw it away when you're done.

17:59.628 --> 18:01.721
Oh, I think you'll wanna throw it away.

18:03.198 --> 18:04.756
- Morning.
- Hey, Alan.

18:04.933 --> 18:07.265
Congratulate me. I'm kind of engaged.

18:07.836 --> 18:10.862
- So she said yes?
- Not exactly.

18:11.039 --> 18:12.904
- You gave her the ring, right?
- Yup.

18:13.075 --> 18:14.099
Well, what did she say?

18:18.480 --> 18:20.311
You had to be there.

18:20.482 --> 18:22.347
Okay. So have you set a date?

18:23.285 --> 18:24.912
- For what?
- The wedding.

18:25.554 --> 18:29.354
What wedding?
Nobody's getting married. I'm just engaged.

18:29.525 --> 18:31.425
When do we get to see this rock?

18:32.227 --> 18:34.787
Well, Chelsea just finished
her second cup of coffee...

18:34.963 --> 18:37.454
...so I'd guess 15, 20 minutes.

18:41.103 --> 18:43.196
Anybody understand
what that was all about?

18:43.372 --> 18:45.465
I think Chelsea swallowed some nickels.

18:53.715 --> 18:55.273
Chelsea?

18:55.450 --> 18:56.974
Yeah?

18:57.152 --> 18:59.416
You've been in there for a while.
How's it going?

18:59.588 --> 19:02.352
Just fine.
- You need any help?

19:02.524 --> 19:05.254
I brought Alan's little poop stool.

19:07.830 --> 19:10.924
Go away.
- All right, all right.

19:11.099 --> 19:14.159
But just remember,
when you hear a metallic clink, stop.

19:14.570 --> 19:16.561
I think I can handle it.

19:16.738 --> 19:21.437
It's not on my homeowner's policy yet,
so if you flush it by mistake, I'm screwed.

19:21.810 --> 19:24.472
Charlie, I swear,
if you don't walk away from that door...

19:24.646 --> 19:28.878
...I will eat a block of cheese,
and you will never see that ring again.

19:29.451 --> 19:32.079
- Okay, I'm walking.
Good.

19:32.254 --> 19:35.417
- Love you.
Don't push it, Charlie.

19:35.591 --> 19:37.115
Right back at you.

19:41.363 --> 19:45.322
Oh, Charlie, it's beautiful.
